<title>JAPAN: Japan June dept store sales fall 4.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan June dept store sales fall 4.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales at department stores in Japan declined 4.7 percent in June from a year earlier to 668.8 billion yen, the Japan Department Stores' Association said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Sales in June declined for the third consecutive month on a year-on-year basis.</p>
<p>Sales for the first half of 1997, meanwhile, rose 0.4 percent to 4.2 trillion yen.</p>
<p>The association said the decline was mainly because consumers remained cautious after the consumption tax was raised to five percent from three percent on April 1.</p>
<p>A series of typhoons that hit Japan had also dampened consumption, the association said.</p>
</text>
